  "schema": "elder-souls/clips@1",
  "owner": "RI-CMB02 §D.3 (root motion is authoritative), RI-CMB01 §C.5, RI-CMB04 §A step 4",
  "units": "rotations are Euler XYZ in DEGREES in the bone's local frame; root_forward is a CUMULATIVE FRACTION of the move's declared displacement; root_offset is metres in the character's local frame",

  "phase_parameterisation": {
    "why": "A clip is authored ONCE as a set of normalised phase curves and INSTANTIATED at each move's own declared frame counts. That keeps the frame data (frames.json / roll.json) the single source of timing while letting the pose be authored where it is legible.",
    "anchors_attack": { "0.0": "animation frame 1", "1.0": "the last STARTUP frame", "2.0": "the last ACTIVE frame", "3.0": "the last RECOVERY frame" },
    "anchors_roll":   { "0.0": "animation frame 1", "1.0": "the last STARTUP frame", "2.0": "the last I-FRAME", "3.0": "the last RECOVERY frame" },
    "anchors_simple": { "0.0": "animation frame 1", "3.0": "the last frame" },
    "interpolation": "smoothstep (3u^2 - 2u^3) between adjacent keys, clamped outside the key range. Deterministic, allocation-free, and NON-LINEAR, which is what makes the per-frame root delta a speed curve rather than a translate (RI-CMB01 M3, RI-CMB02 M3).",
    "not_a_reskin": "RI-CMB02's automatic-fail list forbids 'a single attack animation shared by all weapon classes with the numbers swapped'. Classes therefore select DIFFERENT pose archetypes (cut_diagonal / thrust / chop_overhead / sweep_wide), with per-class amplitude and stance, on top of their own frame counts. The archetype assignment is in each moveset file."
  },

